# What makes a question causal?
subtitle: "Why the effect of insurance on one person can never be observed, and how Oregon's 2008 lottery measured it for a group anyway."
tags: ["causal inference","potential outcomes","health insurance","randomization"]
teaches: ["methods/potential-outcomes","methods/randomization","concepts/selection-bias"]
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed"}
next: {"title":"Why insured people can look sicker: selection bias, decomposed","href":"https://drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/dcast/causal-inference-in-economics-evidence-from-health-and-health-care/why-insured-people-can-look-sicker-selection-bias-decomposed.cast"}

## Her two futures
voice: female
level: basic

    icon maria size 240 x 170 y 410 or ["person"] icon_look picture of woman hidden true
    text maria_name "Maria, 40" x 170 y 225 font_size 58 hidden true
    arrow road1 #2f6b8f from.x 320 from.y 460 to.x 555 to.y 600 style.stroke_width 4 hidden true
    math road1_lab tex "D_i = 1" size 50 x 390 y 625 hidden true
    arrow road0 dashed #b5482e from.x 320 from.y 360 to.x 555 to.y 200 style.stroke_width 4 hidden true
    math road0_lab tex "D_i = 0" size 50 x 390 y 175 hidden true
    shape card1 thick #2f6b8f shape rect x 770 y 610 width 400 height 165 radius 12 hidden true
    text num1 "24 good days" #2f6b8f x 770 y 610 font_size 64 hidden true
    math sym1 tex Y_i(1) size 52 colors {"Y_i(1)":"#2f6b8f"} x 1050 y 610 hidden true
    shape card0 dashed thick #b5482e shape rect x 770 y 190 width 400 height 165 radius 12 hidden true
    text num0 "19 good days" #b5482e x 770 y 190 font_size 64 hidden true
    text q0 "?" #b5482e x 770 y 190 font_size 140 hidden true
    math sym0 tex Y_i(0) size 52 colors {"Y_i(0)":"#b5482e"} x 1050 y 190 hidden true
    math eq tex "\\tau_i = {Y_i(1)} - {Y_i(0)} = 24 - 19 = 5" size 52 colors {"19":"#b5482e","24":"#2f6b8f","{Y_i(1)}":"#2f6b8f","{Y_i(0)}":"#b5482e","\\tau_i":"#8a5fa8"} x 770 y 400 hidden true
    figure fig aspect 3:2 members ["maria","maria_name","road1","road1_lab","road0","road0_lab","card1","num1","sym1","card0","num0","q0","sym0","eq"] hidden true

    card title "Her two futures"

When we say health insurance improved someone's health, what exactly are we comparing?
    draw maria

We'll answer it in three steps: one woman, then  (@highlight maria@)a table of four people, then a lottery of ninety thousand.
    draw maria_name

Start with the woman: Maria is forty, on a low income, and she gets Medicaid. Call that D equals one.
    draw road1 road1_lab

A year on, she counts twenty-four good days out of the last thirty. Our numbers are made up, to keep the idea plain.
    draw card1 num1 sym1

Most people would stop there: she's covered, she feels well, so coverage worked.
    highlight num1 effect circle

But well compared with what?
    draw road0 road0_lab

Compared with the same woman, in the same year, without coverage. Say she'd have had nineteen good days.
    draw card0 num0 sym0

Insurance's effect on her is the gap between her own two futures: five good days.
    draw eq

That is what the sentence means: Maria with coverage against Maria without, not against her neighbour.
    highlight card1 card0

And here is the catch. She did get coverage, so only one of those futures ever happened.
    fade road0 road0_lab card0 sym0 to 0.3

The nineteen was never measured, and it  (@draw q0@)never can be, because nobody can rewind her year.
    hide num0

So her effect is perfectly well defined, and no data set will ever contain it.
    morph eq tex "\\tau_i = 24 - \\;?\\; = \\;?"

What data hold is one number per person: t (@highlight card1@)he future that her D picked.
    morph eq tex "Y_i = D_i\\,{Y_i(1)} + (1 - D_i)\\,{Y_i(0)}"

    quiz "Maria's neighbour James has no coverage and 25 good days. What did insurance do for Maria?" intro "A quick check."
        right: We can't tell: twenty-five is James's life without coverage, and the number Maria's effect needs is her own, which is missing.
        wrong: Whose life is the twenty-five from, and whose missing number would the effect need?
        * It cost her one good day
        * Nothing at all
        + We can't tell from these numbers

That missing future is what makes a question causal: it asks about something no one will ever see.
    highlight q0 effect circle

## The column that is always blank
voice: female
level: basic

    text h_person "Person" x 150 y 665 font_size 46 hidden true
    math h_d tex D_i size 50 x 360 y 665 hidden true
    math h_y1 tex Y_i(1) size 50 colors {"Y_i(1)":"#2f6b8f"} x 560 y 665 hidden true
    math h_y0 tex Y_i(0) size 50 colors {"Y_i(0)":"#b5482e"} x 760 y 665 hidden true
