audio:
  lang: en
  lines:
    female|a||When we say health insurance improved someone's health, what exactly are we comparing?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6360
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'female|a||We''ll answer it in three steps: one woman, then a table of four people, then a lottery of ninety thousand.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:cyne50'
    'female|a||Start with the woman: Maria is forty, on a low income, and she gets Medicaid. Call that D equals one.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1th0y7v'
    female|a||A year on, she counts twenty-four good days out of the last thirty. Our numbers are made up, to keep the idea plain.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:9n5llw'
    'female|a||Most people would stop there: she''s covered, she feels well, so coverage worked.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:n457e1'
    female|a||But well compared with what?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 2400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:ie64ko'
    female|a||Compared with the same woman, in the same year, without coverage. Say she'd have had nineteen good days.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1mbpeyr'
    'female|a||Insurance''s effect on her is the gap between her own two futures: five good days.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1gqvtzu'
    'female|a||That is what the sentence means: Maria with coverage against Maria without, not against her neighbour.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:7hbpqn'
    female|a||And here is the catch. She did get coverage, so only one of those futures ever happened.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:11gkmpw'
    female|a||The nineteen was never measured, and it never can be, because nobody can rewind her year.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:68sm5x'
    female|a||So her effect is perfectly well defined, and no data set will ever contain it.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:93imor'
    'female|a||What data hold is one number per person: the future that her D picked.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:wk14oc'
    female|a||A quick check. Maria's neighbour James has no coverage and 25 good days. What did insurance do for Maria?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:g2z6bo'
    'female|a||We can''t tell: twenty-five is James''s life without coverage, and the number Maria''s effect needs is her own, which is missing.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8880
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'female|a||That missing future is what makes a question causal: it asks about something no one will ever see.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6800
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||So let's pretend, just this once, that we could see both futures, for four people.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5800
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Maria's row holds her twenty-four and her nineteen, and the gap between them, five.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:e1q71a'
    female|a||James, Rosa and Daniel get two numbers each. Rosa is the sickest of the four, and James and Daniel the healthiest.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1etwxwf'
    'female|a||Their own effects run down the last column: four, three and four good days. Those who will sign up gain four on average, the same as everyone.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:z0fscb'
    female|a||Averaged over the four, coverage adds four good days a month. Economists call that the average treatment effect.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:paxjij'
    'female|a||But in the real world, nobody shows us both columns: each of them chose whether to sign up.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:18qxnhp'
    female|a||The two in worse health, Maria and Rosa, signed up. James and Daniel didn't bother.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1991ams'
    female|a||So for Maria and Rosa we see only the coverage column, and for James and Daniel only the other one.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6800
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:fguxpz'
    female|a||And the effect column, the one we came for, goes blank all the way down.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 4720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:9qwen6'
    female|a||Half the table is missing, and which half depends on what each person chose. That is why a causal question is a missing-data problem.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:p3oc7o'
    'female|a||A survey fills the gap the obvious way: it compares the insured with the uninsured.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:kew4ml'
    female|a||Before the sum, a prediction. The two sicker people signed up. Will the survey's gap, insured minus uninsured, come out above the true four days, below it, or about the same?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 12520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:4h4xo9'
    'female|a||Below: the people who signed up started out sicker, so their numbers sit low whatever coverage did for them.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6960
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||The insured, Maria and Rosa, average twenty-one good days. The uninsured average twenty-five.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7120
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||So the survey says coverage costs four good days, when on average it adds four.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:o9x365'
    'female|a||That gap of eight is not insurance at all. It is who chose it: the insured started out eight days sicker.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:f0l210'
    female|a||To borrow honestly, we'd need uninsured people who differ from the insured in nothing but the coverage.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1wrj14l'
    female|a||So where would we find uninsured people just like the insured? In 2008, Oregon made some.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7440
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||The state had money to add about ten thousand adults to Medicaid, and about ninety thousand put their names down.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1rwbknw'
    'female|a||So it drew names by lottery: about thirty thousand were drawn and invited to apply. Call being drawn Z equals one.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1ixa5ol'
    female|a||A lottery knows nothing about anyone's health, so on average each side gets the same mix of Marias and Daniels.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7800
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:d8yc86'
    female|a||Picture our four people copied thousands of times, and split by the draw.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1amx6g5'
    'female|a||On average, both sides would score twenty-five good days with coverage and twenty-one without: the averages from our table.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:o8rmwa'
    'female|a||Keep it a toy for now: everyone drawn enrols, and nobody else gets coverage. So each side lives only one future.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:isfa7i'
    female|a||The drawn side's life without coverage is a blank, just like Maria's.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 4320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1i6lhpk'
    female|a||But because chance alone chose the sides, the other side's twenty-one can stand in for it.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:tdbvye'
    'female|a||Twenty-five minus twenty-one: four good days, the true average effect, though nobody''s own effect was ever seen.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1i63d9q'
    'female|a||The survey, with the same kind of people, said minus four. The only thing that changed is who decided: a person, or a draw.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:17e0l5e'
    'female|a||Now the real wrinkle: in Oregon, only about three in ten of those drawn ended up enrolled.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1pyzmun'
    'female|a||In our toy, that pulls the drawn side down to about twenty-two, and the plain gap shrinks to about one point two: the effect of the offer.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1sbs12r'
    'female|a||So the gap from the offer, divided by the rise in enrolment the draw caused, gives back four: the effect of coverage for the people the draw moved onto it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:12rdgu6'
    'female|a||But a draw can be unlucky too: with only four people, the two sides could easily differ by chance.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6800
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||So how far off is each method as the groups grow? Across, people on each side; up, the typical miss in good days.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:gu06g5'
    female|a||The survey is off by eight good days, because the sicker people chose coverage, and asking more people changes nothing about that.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:c71zua'
    female|a||A lottery is off only by chance. If good days vary by about ten from person to person, two people a side can miss by ten.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:15tgfvz'
    female|a||Watch the point slide to bigger groups, and see how far off each method stays.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:fcznxq'
    female|a||The lottery's miss falls toward zero, while the survey's stays at eight.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5480
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'female|a||It shrinks with the square root of the group: four times the people, half the miss.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:19g89wz'
    female|a||With six thousand a side, about the size of Oregon's health survey, chance is worth less than a quarter of a good day.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:um7gvc'
    female|a||So the survey's problem is who chose, not how many it asked.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:oo9xug'
    female|a||More data shrinks the noise of chance. It cannot undo a choice.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 4960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1cetrf1'
    female|a||Oregon's real margins were wider than this toy's, partly because most winners never enrolled. But they were margins of chance, and they shrink with numbers.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:k2nxt5'
    female|a||So a big lottery leaves only a small, honest margin of error, and that is the kind of number Oregon could report.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1jn7sug'
    female|a||So what did Oregon's draw show about coverage itself?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 4400
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||In the first year, those drawn used more care, had less medical debt, and said they felt healthier.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1p2dl71'
    female|a||About two years in, researchers interviewed and examined some twelve thousand people in and around Portland.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:dlirl8'
    'female|a||Each row is the effect of coverage itself for the people the draw moved onto it: the offer''s gap divided by the rise in enrolment. The dashed line is no effect.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:rpm7vw'
    'female|a||Depression: about nine points lower, from a base of thirty percent, and its range of plausible values stays clear of zero.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1vbb71h'
    'female|a||Catastrophic medical bills: about four and a half points lower, and clear of zero too.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:d1owx5'
    'female|a||Blood pressure and blood sugar: close to zero, with ranges that run past it on both sides.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1nops1x'
    female|a||And here economists read the same row differently.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 3600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:16t4wvo'
    female|a||Some take it as evidence that coverage did not lower blood sugar within two years.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 4960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:xzg0m6'
    female|a||Others note that only about one person in twenty had high blood sugar at all, so the range is too wide to rule out a worthwhile effect.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:ngjws2'
    'female|a||And they point to what did move: new diabetes diagnoses and diabetes medicine rose clearly among the covered.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:ivvwwi'
    female|a||What would tell the two readings apart is many more people with diabetes, followed for longer, so that the range of chance shrinks.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:rm4voe'
    female|a||One new case. A hospital wants to know whether a follow-up phone call after discharge keeps patients from coming back. Which comparison answers it?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1a1oi5c'
    'female|a||Picked at random: then nothing but the call separates the two groups, so each can stand in for the other''s missing future.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7880
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||So what were we comparing when we said insurance improved her health? Maria with coverage, against Maria without.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8400
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||One of those futures is always missing, for everyone, and no amount of data brings it back.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1qrmtav'
    female|a||What we can do is borrow it, and a lottery makes the borrowing fair, on average and within a margin of chance.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1vkgfor'
    female|a||Whether coverage helped Maria herself, we will never know. Whether it helps people like her, who sign up when coverage is offered, Oregon's draw began to answer.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:ffhsf3'
    female|a||Whose life is the twenty-five from, and whose missing number would the effect need?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6640
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Yes.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 800
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Right.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 1040
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||That's it.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 1000
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Exactly.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 1200
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Spot on.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 1160
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||You got it.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 960
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Quite right.:
